  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Chop the stale bread into bite-sized pieces and toast until crispy.",
    "Caramelize the chopped onions in coconut oil until golden brown.",
    "Add the jerk seasoning, allspice, brown sugar, and korean chili flakes to the onions and stir until combined.",
    "Add the halal chicken broth and bring to a boil, then reduce heat to a simmer.",
    "Add the toasted bread, chopped red bell pepper, and green onion to the braising liquid and cook for 10 minutes.",
    "Transfer the bread mixture to a Korean brass bowl and garnish with chopped scallions and extra green onion for serving.",
    "Bake the bread bowl in the preheated oven for an additional 5 minutes, or until crispy and golden brown.",
    "Serve hot and enjoy!",
    "Optional: Serve with a side of coconut flakes or chopped scallions for added crunch and flavor."
  ],
